comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T14:33:59.739Z","harness:claude-code","Disposition of the 61 pre-existing entries, 2026-08-11 (this item's fifth criterion). The defect turned CI red on the commit that introduced it, and not through the assurance gates themselves: the 61 unknown-author entries were classified actionable, which flipped the storage health check from ok to warn and tripped tracker-measurement-gate twice at once - health_check:storage declared 0 observed 1 (ceiling_exceeded) and validate_warning:validate_history_unknown_author_events declared null observed 61 (undeclared_population). An A/B against the pre-commit tracker isolated it exactly: actionable_unknown_event_count 0 to 61, with provenance_invalid_values and tombstone counts byte-identical on both sides, so no legacy data was involved. Resolved with the supported mechanism rather than by weakening a bound: pm history-author-acknowledge --all-actionable attributed all 61 to harness:claude-code, which is read directly from each event's own agent_harness field rather than inferred. Storage returned to ok, validate returned to its original five warning classes, and the ratchet passed at 30 enforced. That closes the residual half only. Recurrence is still open: the next assurance write will mint another unknown-author entry and re-break the same two bounds, which is why this item stays open on the write-path fix."
  "2026-08-11T22:18:14.387Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-12: assurance registry writes and durable gate verdicts now use the settings-aware detected-author resolver. Full coverage passed at exact 100/100/100/100; static, contracts, packed dogfood, npx, and package ecosystem smoke passed. Temporary acceptance made an assurance mutation without --author and pm activity recorded harness:codex, proving author and provenance agree while the unresolved-author negative path remains covered."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T22:18:14.875Z","harness:codex",Provenance beside an unknown author is not sufficient auditability; the canonical author field must be resolved by the same settings and harness precedence used by other mutations.
